cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Stability Is Not Evidence: Shrinkage Artefacts in a Pre-Registered Neural Value-at-Risk Study"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen data, pre-registration record and execution ledger for a pre-registered
  Value-at-Risk study that produced four apparently well-supported findings and withdrew
  all four. Includes the analytical and synthetic demonstration that shrinkage-induced
  stability is not evidence of a good prior, and the scale-matched permutation control
  that detects it.
